      "output": "Local checks have determined that the version of sudo installed on the remote host is prior to 1.9.5p2.\n\nInstalled version : 1.8.31\nFixed version    : 1.9.5p2\n\nSudo before 1.9.5p2 contains an off-by-one error that can result in a heap-based buffer overflow, which allows privilege escalation to root via 'sudoedit -s' and a command-line argument that ends with a single backslash character. This vulnerability is known as 'Baron Samedit' (CVE-2021-3156).",
